<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Polemonid Pontus</h1><p class="st-meta">37 BCE – 62 CE</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Polemonid Pontus, a Roman client kingdom on the Black Sea ruled by Polemon I, his queen Pythodorida and their son.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 37 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a> made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polemon-i-of-pontus">Polemon</a>, son of the orator <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeno-of-laodicea">Zeno of Laodicea</a>, king of part of the former <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-pontus">Kingdom of Pontus</a>. Polemon kept his throne after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-actium">Actium</a> by switching to Augustus and was also made king of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/bosporan-kingdom">Bosporan Kingdom</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom covered the eastern Pontic coast and inland valleys, including <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/trapezus">Trapezus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zela">Zela</a>. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polemon-i-of-pontus">Polemon</a> was killed c. 8 BCE, his widow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pythodoris">Pythodorida</a>, a granddaughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a>, ruled in her own name for many years. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strabo">Strabo</a>, a native of the region, praised her government.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caligula">Caligula</a> gave the kingdom to her grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polemon-ii-of-pontus">Polemon II</a> in 38 CE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nero">Nero</a> deposed him in 62 CE and annexed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-pontus">Pontus</a> to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 37 BCE – 62 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:58.97%;width:1.97%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>37 BCE – 62 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Polemon I, Pythodorida, Polemon II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Greek religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Pontus (Polemonid)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=12&amp;focus=polemonid-pontus" aria-label="Polemonid Pontus on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5532 792 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Polemonid Pontus lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5879 982h0M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5852 1048h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5852 1048h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Turkey. <a href="/atlas?year=12&amp;focus=polemonid-pontus">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
